A young Gnome warlock named Fizzlewhizzle trudged through the humid jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, his tiny green fingers clutching a battered spellbook. At his side floated Lila, his mischievous succubus pet, her wings fluttering with impatience. As they approached a bandit camp, Lila giggled and whispered, "Let me handle this, darling. I’ll charm the leader for you." With a wink, she swooped in, casting her beguiling magic and turning the bandits into giggling fools. Fizzlewhizzle finished off the dazed enemies with a shadow bolt, grinning at Lila’s efficiency. Yet, back in Orgrimmar, he’d often seen warlocks summoning imposing voidwalkers instead. But here, with Lila’s charm and handiness in battle, he wondered why more didn’t choose succubi.

**Answer:**  
Because succubi have the "Seduction" ability, which can charm humanoids, making them invaluable for solo play and crowd control—especially for quests and grinding, even if voidwalkers are more visually impressive or tanky. [end of text]


